# Cloudflare Pages header rules. Jekyll would skip a leading-underscore file, so
# `_headers` is listed under `include:` in _config.yml to get it copied into _site.
#
# RFC 8288 Link headers let a client discover the sitemap and the llms.txt summary
# without parsing HTML — which is the point for anything that fetches with HEAD or
# doesn't run a parser at all.
#
# The root rule repeats the sitemap link rather than relying on it being inherited
# from /*: Cloudflare merges matching rules, and a same-named header from a more
# specific rule can replace rather than append. Spelling both out on / makes the
# result the same either way. RFC 8288 permits multiple comma-separated values.

/*
  Link: </sitemap.xml>; rel="sitemap"; type="application/xml"

/
  Link: </sitemap.xml>; rel="sitemap"; type="application/xml", </llms.txt>; rel="alternate"; type="text/plain"
